CONTROLS:

Spells - yuiop for spell slots
Use Weapon - t or h
Inventory - 1 through 9 for item slots, or use mouse to manage (right click to drag/drop item)
Using stairs, picking up items - Simply stop on top of them without pressing any weapon or spell keys

To change the games resolution/toggle fullscreen and other settings, edit runtime/settings.yaml.

DEVELOPMENT:

The game is actively seeking new contributors! Shoot me an email at adam.domurad@gmail.com if interested and I'll happily help you get started.

COMPILING

Lanarts builds with CMake (3.24 or newer) and a C++14 compiler. Most libraries are downloaded
at configure time, pinned to exact releases; you need these from your system:

  macOS:          brew install cmake sdl2 sdl2_image sdl2_mixer freetype
  Debian/Ubuntu:  apt install cmake libsdl2-dev libsdl2-image-dev libsdl2-mixer-dev libfreetype-dev
  Python 3 (to generate runtime/compiled/Resources.lua during the build)

FreeType is downloaded and built too when the system has none.

To build and run, from the lanarts source folder:
  ./run.sh              debug build
  ./run.sh -O           optimised build
  ./run.sh --headless   no graphics or sound (for simulations, see tools/sim)
The other options are listed at the top of run.sh.

Or use the CMake presets directly (CMakePresets.json; IDEs such as CLion and VS Code pick them up):
  cmake --preset release
  cmake --build --preset release
  cd runtime && ../build/release/src/lanarts

Tests: ./run.sh --headless --build && ctest --preset headless

Web (Emscripten): ./run.sh --web --build, from a shell where emcmake is available.
Windows: cross-compile with ./run.sh --mingw --build (MinGW-w64 with SDL2 and FreeType packages),
or open the folder in an IDE with CMake support and run the game from the 'runtime' folder.
